 ### [Fixed-Point Volume Ray Casting](12056-fixed-point-volume-ray-casting.md)
-Fixed-Point Volume Ray Casting is a direct volume rendering technique that replaces standard floating-point arithmetic with fixed-point operations for interpolation and accumulation to improve computational efficiency [G]. It is specifically implemented in the Visualization Toolkit (VTK) via the `vtkFixedPointVolumeRayCastMapper` class [G]. Unlike general-purpose ray casting which may rely on hardware floating-point units, this method optimizes performance by intercepting decimal parts and using integer-based arithmetic, making it particularly suitable for large-scale volumetric datasets such as seismic or medical images where memory bandwidth and CPU cycles are constrained [G]. It builds on the standard front-to-back compositing algorithm but introduces optimizations like `MinMaxVolume` generation to skip empty voxels [G].
