 ### CPU Volume Transport (Multi-Ray)
-**Definition**: Solves transport for multiple rays in parallel on CPU by iterating over rays and calling the single-ray solver for each [G].
-**Step**: Loop ray from 0 to `num_rays` - 1. Calculate `offset = ray * num_samples`. Call `solve_one_ray` with `sigma + offset`, `source + offset`, `num_samples`, `ds`, and `initial_intensity[ray]`. Store result in `output[ray]` [G].
-**Layout**: Input arrays `sigma`, `source`, `initial_intensity` are row-major `[ray][sample]`. Output array `output` is `[ray]` [G].
